From 70edba0d6ea369d9e5767658ede5c61a11492340 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: v <a@b>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 14:48:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] ASoC: codecs: wsa884x: write the cached PA gain when the
 slave attaches

The reset gain that patch 0001 put into wsa884x_defaults only exists in
the regmap cache. The amplifier itself powers up with CSR gain 2, which
"PA Volume" reads back as 29 (+34.5 dB). Nothing guarantees that value
reaches the hardware:

 - after a cold boot the cache is not dirty (no cache-only write has
   happened yet), so regcache_sync() returns without writing;
 - after a re-attach regcache_mark_dirty() sets no_sync_defaults, so the
   sync skips every register whose cached value equals its table default,
   which is exactly the 0 dB value;
 - setting "PA Volume" to its already-cached value is a no-op in
   regmap_update_bits(), so user space cannot repair it either.

The only write that happened to carry the gain was the read-modify-write
of the GAIN_EN bit in wsa884x_set_gain_parameters(), and only when the
compander port is disabled at that moment.

Write DRE_CTL_1 explicitly from the cache in wsa884x_init(), before the
gain parameters are applied. The register is not volatile, so the read
returns the cached intended value (0 dB, or what user space set within
the machine driver limit).

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5
---
 sound/soc/codecs/wsa884x.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/wsa884x.c b/sound/soc/codecs/wsa884x.c
index eed036602..bb440247c 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/wsa884x.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/wsa884x.c
@@ -1520,6 +1520,7 @@ static void wsa884x_init(struct wsa884x_priv *wsa884x)
 {
 	unsigned int wo_ctl_0;
 	unsigned int variant = 0;
+	unsigned int gain;
 
 	if (!regmap_read(wsa884x->regmap, WSA884X_OTP_REG_0, &variant))
 		variant = variant & WSA884X_OTP_REG_0_ID_MASK;
@@ -1539,6 +1540,16 @@ static void wsa884x_init(struct wsa884x_priv *wsa884x)
 				       WSA884X_ANA_WO_CTL_0_PA_AUX_0_DB);
 	regmap_write(wsa884x->regmap, WSA884X_ANA_WO_CTL_0, wo_ctl_0);
 
+	/*
+	 * The cache holds the intended PA gain (0 dB unless user space lowered
+	 * it), but the amplifier is at its power-on gain here. After a cold boot
+	 * the cache is not dirty and regcache_sync() writes nothing; after a
+	 * re-attach it skips values equal to the table default. Write the cached
+	 * value explicitly so the hardware never keeps +34.5 dB.
+	 */
+	if (!regmap_read(wsa884x->regmap, WSA884X_DRE_CTL_1, &gain))
+		regmap_write(wsa884x->regmap, WSA884X_DRE_CTL_1, gain);
+
 	wsa884x_set_gain_parameters(wsa884x);
 
 	wsa884x->hw_init = true;
